                    <p>Startup Registration (DPIIT Recognition) gets your company officially recognised as a startup under Startup India. It unlocks 3-year income tax exemption (Section 80IAC), 80% patent fee reduction, 50% trademark reduction, self-certification under 9 labour and 3 environmental laws, Seed Fund access, and angel tax abolition (FY 2026). Filed on NSWS (nsws.gov.in) with zero fee. However, approximately 70% of applications are rejected due to weak innovation statements.</p><div class="table-responsive-wrapper" style="margin-top:16px;"><table><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Scheme</td><td>Startup India (launched 16 January 2016)</td></tr><tr><td>Authority</td><td>DPIIT, Ministry of Commerce and Industry</td></tr><tr><td>Portal</td><td>NSWS (nsws.gov.in) or startupindia.gov.in</td></tr><tr><td>Eligible Entities</td><td>Pvt Ltd | LLP | Registered Partnership Firm</td></tr><tr><td>Eligibility</td><td>&lt; 10 years | Turnover &lt; Rs 100 Cr | Innovation/scalability</td></tr><tr><td>Govt Fee</td><td>ZERO - completely free</td></tr><tr><td>Key Benefits</td><td>3-year tax holiday (S.80IAC) | 80% patent | 50% trademark | Self-cert | Seed Fund</td></tr><tr><td>Processing Time</td><td>2-10 working days</td></tr></tbody></table></div></p>
                </div>
                <p>Gurugram is India's startup capital. DLF Cyber City houses unicorn HQs. Sohna Road is the SaaS corridor. Manesar IMT hosts deeptech. Yet many startups lack DPIIT recognition - leaving lakhs in tax savings unclaimed. A startup with Rs 50 lakh profit saves approximately Rs 15 lakh over the 3-year Section 80IAC exemption. 70% of applications are rejected for weak innovation statements. Learn more about <a href="/startup-registration">Startup Registration across India</a>.</p>
