<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is Startup Registration (DPIIT Recognition)</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>Startup Registration (DPIIT Recognition) is the process by which a Private Limited Company, LLP, or Registered Partnership Firm obtains official recognition as a 'startup' from DPIIT under the Startup India initiative, by filing an application on the NSWS portal demonstrating eligibility criteria of age, turnover, innovation, and scalability.</p><p>The recognition results in a DPIIT Certificate of Recognition - a government-issued certificate serving as proof of startup status for tax benefits, IP fee reductions, compliance relaxations, government funding, and investor credibility. For Gurugram startups seeking angel or VC funding, DPIIT recognition is increasingly a baseline credibility marker.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Startup Registration in Gurugram:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>DPIIT:</strong> Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade - evaluates and grants startup recognition under Ministry of Commerce and Industry.</p><p><strong>Section 80IAC:</strong> 100% profit deduction for 3 consecutive years within first 10 years. Only Pvt Ltd and LLPs. Application to Inter-Ministerial Board after DPIIT recognition.</p><p><strong>Innovation Statement:</strong> The narrative explaining how the product/service/process is genuinely new and technology-driven. The #1 rejection factor when poorly written.</p><p><strong>NSWS:</strong> National Single Window System (nsws.gov.in) - current filing platform for DPIIT recognition.</p><p><strong>Self-Certification:</strong> DPIIT-recognised startups self-certify under 9 labour + 3 environmental laws for 3-5 years without inspections.</p>

